{
  "An accordion opens and closes sections under their headers: one at a time or several, kept open, with icons, three looks and sections built when they are first opened.": "",
  "An `<AccordionItem>`'s children are its section. `value` lists the open items' keys and `x-model` binds it two-way. Created with `new`, items are added and removed programmatically.": "",
  "One or several open": "",
  "One item is open at a time; with `multiple` several can be. `collapsible={false}` keeps one open: its header cannot close it.": "",
  "Lazy sections": "",
  "A section is built when it is first opened and kept afterwards (`lazy`, on by default). An item with a `content` factory and `keepAlive={false}` has its content disposed when it closes and made again when it opens.": "",
  "From header to header, and into an open section.": "",
  "Opens or closes the focused item.": "",
  "The next / previous header, wrapping around (with `arrowKeys`).": "",
  "The first / last header (with `arrowKeys`).": "",
  "Focuses that header and opens or closes it (Control + Option + key on Apple platforms).": "",
  "A `<button>` with `aria-expanded` and `aria-controls`, inside an element with `role=\"heading\"` and `aria-level` (`headingLevel`).": "",
  "`role=\"region\"` named by its header (`aria-labelledby`) while there are six items or fewer, as the APG suggests; `regions` decides.": "",
  "`visibility: hidden` once closed: out of the Tab order and the accessibility tree.": "",
  "With `collapsible` off, the header of the item that may not close has `aria-disabled=\"true\"`.": "",
  "The height animates with the motion tokens; reduced motion turns it off.": "",
  "The root. `data-variant`, `data-size`, `data-chevron`, `data-disabled`.": "",
  "An item: `data-expanded`, `data-disabled`.": "",
  "The heading and the button in it.": "",
  "The parts of a header.": "",
  "The section (animated) and its content.": "",
  "Header sizes, from the density tokens.": "",
  "Units: the accordion and its items per variant (`list`, `list-next`, `separated`, `flush`; `expanded`).": "",
  "Units: a header (`expanded`, `hover`, `pressed`, `disabled`, `focus`), its icon, the chevron (`open`) and a plate behind it, the open section.": "",
  "The chevron’s and the plate’s sizes; the space above and below a section's content.": "",
  "Accordion props": "",
  "The open items' keys (an item without a key: its index). `x-model` binds it two-way.": "",
  "Several items can be open; otherwise opening one closes the other.": "",
  "`false`: one item stays open; its header has `aria-disabled` while it may not close.": "",
  "The `aria-level` of the headers (1 to 6): fit it to the headings around.": "",
  "Up, Down, Home and End move between the headers.": "",
  "Sections are `role=\"region\"` landmarks; `auto` while there are six items or fewer.": "",
  "`list` (one bordered box), `separated` (a card per item), `flush` (lines only).": "",
  "Where the open/closed arrow sits: `end`, `start`, `none`.": "",
  "A section is built when first opened, then kept. An item's own `lazy` wins.": "",
  "`false`: what an item's `content` made is disposed when it closes and made again when it opens. An item's own `keepAlive` wins.": "",
  "AccordionItem props": "",
  "The header text; `&Shipping` makes Alt+S open or close it. The same property as `text`.": "",
  "Names the item in `value`. The JSX `key` works too.": "",
  "Whether the section is open.": "",
  "A tooltip on the header.": "",
  "the Accordion": "",
  "This item's own setting.": "",
  "Makes the section content when it is built: instead of, or after, the JSX children.": "",
  "A disabled item cannot be opened or closed; a hidden one is left out.": "",
  "The items, in order.": "",
  "The open items.": "",
  "Whether its section has been built.": "",
  "Its `Accordion`, its header button, its region.": "",
  "Adds an item. An item of another `Accordion` moves here.": "",
  "Removes the item and disposes it; focus inside moves to a neighbour.": "",
  "Programmatically. `expandAll` needs `multiple`; with `collapsible` off one item stays open.": "",
  "As a click would: the cancelable events run. `item.expanded = true` sets it programmatically.": "",
  "An item focuses its header.": "",
  "The user is about to open / close an item. `e`: `{ item, index, cancel, source, event? }`; `e.cancel = true` leaves it.": "",
  "An item opened / closed. `e`: `{ item, index, byUser, source }`.": "",
  "The accordion writes no text of its own, so it has nothing in `uiLocale`.": ""
}
